# Overview

<design figma-url="https://www.figma.com/design/tLYtw0hYKA22PTU3TH2r7r/?node-id=6110:101933">

![Spacing - banner](https://zeroheight-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/d0511ec89dd444a8b4a1c6?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=AKIA3AVNYHQKYPFHNVW5%2F20260530%2Feu-west-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260530T145142Z&X-Amz-Expires=604800&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Signature=c4bec39f702d1123bcd3682b2edd67320b1df5f53d9d137a8dd50bf37a904af2)

**Spacing - banner**

</design>

## About

Spacing and sizing are basic principles that establish visual consistency, create balance, and guide user focus. By defining the size of components and the space between them, the Salesforce Lightning Design System ensures a harmonious and scalable user interface that adapts seamlessly across devices and screen sizes.

### Spacing

Spacing controls the empty areas around or within components, such as margins, padding, and gaps between elements. Effective spacing improves readability, reduces visual clutter, and enhances usability. 

Spacing defines these visual aspects of a page.

* Proper alignment of components.
* Clear differentiation of grouped and unrelated elements.
* White space that directs user attention to key content or actions.

<design figma-url="https://www.figma.com/design/tLYtw0hYKA22PTU3TH2r7r/?node-id=6114:102372">

![Overview-spacing](https://zeroheight-uploads.s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/3dbfc0c6648842bdef4454?X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=AKIA3AVNYHQKYPFHNVW5%2F20260530%2Feu-west-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260530T145142Z&X-Amz-Expires=604800&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Signature=5cae34ef1b31fcaf8f46333c2527dba70e6330bb8ee453ac860fc3bbd51af2a0)

**Overview-spacing**

<notes>

Spacing in styling hooks refers to padding or margins around an element. 

</notes>

</design>

### Sizing

Sizing refers to the dimensions of a component, such as height, width, or size variants. When sizes are consistent, it's easier for users to predict where things will be on the page. This predictability makes the interface easier to use.

A design system applies sizing in a few key ways.

* Defines the physical dimensions of elements like buttons, icons, and cards.
* Provides scalable size options (small, medium, large) to accommodate different contexts.
* Supports responsiveness to make sure that designs function well on all screen sizes.

